# Requires the multi-user ACL engine (compat/delta.md item 1, deferred to the ACL workstream).
Script ACL check
# macOS `leaks` reports allocations retained by the Lua scripting path — tracked as debt in
# compat/delta.md (scripting-leak note); Linux CI does not run this check.
Check for memory leaks
# CLIENT LIST polled from inside a running script cannot observe concurrent session changes yet.
Timedout scripts and unblocked command
# SCRIPT KILL lacks the UNKILLABLE distinction for scripts that already wrote.
Timedout scripts that modified data can't be killed by SCRIPT KILL
# Script-timeout BUSY semantics: PeaDB aborts a pure-Lua timed-out script instead of staying BUSY.
SHUTDOWN NOSAVE can kill a timedout script anyway
# Blocked-client pops served by the unblock path are not yet propagated to replicas.
Replication of script multiple pushes to list with BLPOP
# SELECT inside a script is not reflected in captured effects replication.
Lua scripts using SELECT are replicated correctly
# The LDB (Lua debugger) session protocol is not implemented (SCRIPT DEBUG is accepted as a no-op).
Test scripting debug protocol parsing
Test scripting debug lua stack overflow
# Replica-mode script gating (MASTERDOWN for EVAL under replica-serve-stale-data no,
# no-writes shebang on replicas) not implemented yet — replication/scripting workstream.
allow-stale shebang flag
no-writes shebang flag on replica
# Replica handshake cannot complete while a script blocks the event loop (busy-script I/O semantics).
not enough good replicas state change during long script
